  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta \n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{3}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta }=\\frac{{sec}^{3}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta }\n$$\n\nWe now simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{3}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}}\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{\\cancel{{sec}^{2}\u2061\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sec}^{3}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{1+{tan}^{2}\u2061\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta .\n$$",
